  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Women-Owned Small Business set-aside contracts obligated $925M in FY2026 to date across 2,578 awards. The average award size was $359K, and obligations were down 27.5% year over year. Fiscal history shows obligations of $856M in FY21, $934M in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $1.3B in FY25, with the current fiscal-year total at $925M. The Department of Defense led buying with $390M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $122M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $115M. Other significant agency buyers included the Department of Commerce at $73.8M and the Department of Justice at $40.7M. Other Computer Related Services received $170M in obligations, and Engineering Services received $143M. Top vendors included FCN, INC. at $24.4M and BLACK CANYON CONSULTING LLC at $23.5M. Note that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have WOSB set-aside obligations changed over recent years?",
        "body": "Obligations peaked in FY24 and FY25 at $1.3B and then fell to $925M in FY26 to date. Obligations were down 27.5% year over year. Obligations in earlier years were $1.2B in FY23, $934M in FY22, and $856M in FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries are the largest buyers of WOSB set-asides?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $390M in FY2026 to date, the largest buyer. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $122M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $115M. Other Computer Related Services led industries with $170M, and Engineering Services followed with $143M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through WOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $925M through WOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. The program produced 2,578 awards with an average award size of $359K. Historical totals were $856M in FY21, $934M in FY22, $1.2B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $1.3B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use WOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense uses WOSB set-asides the most, obligating $390M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $122M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $115M. Other notable buyers included the Department of Commerce at $73.8M and the Department of Justice at $40.7M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest WOSB set-aside contractors?",
      "a": "FCN, INC. was the largest WOSB set-aside contractor in FY2026 to date with $24.4M in obligations. BLACK CANYON CONSULTING LLC followed with $23.5M, and SOFTWARE INFORMATION RESOURCE CORP. followed with $20.8M."
